"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","doi":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2022.111964","year":2022,"record_id":"MLDB-003209","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The 1-octanol/water partition constant (logPO/W) of complexes 1 and 2 in the 1-octanol/PBS system was evaluated by the shake flask method. Solutions of complexes 1 and 2 (30, 40 and 50 μM) were dissolved in PBS solution that pre-saturated with 1-octanol. An equal volume (2.0 mL) of the solution was mixed with 1-octanol that pre-saturated with PBS and shaken at room temperature for 12 h, and then centrifuged into PBS and octanol phases at 2500 rpm. The concentration at 0 h and 12 h in the PBS phase was measured by UV–Vis spectrophotometry. The value of logP was calculated from the average of three independent measurements by the formula: log Po/w = log[(Cinitial - Cfinal)/Cfinal]"}],"ccdc":["SEPLIM"]}